2. Anything taken and preserved as a memorial of victory, as arms, flags, or standards captured from an enemy.

{{smaller block|And for a ''trophy'' brought the Giant's coat away,
Made of the beards of Kings.
{{right|''Drayton'', Polyolbion, iv. 317.}}}}

{{smaller block|Over the chimney-piece was a small mirror, and above that the ''trophy'' of a fox's brush.
