3. Something regarded as a memorial or evidence of victory; a prize.

{{smaller block|This is that famoused ''trophy'' which Philip would have his son Alexander in the games of Olympus to wrestle for.
{{right|''Ford'', Honour Triumphant, ii.}}}}

4. A memorial; a memento.

{{smaller block|The mere word 's a slave
Debosh'd on every tomb, on every grave
A lying ''trophy''.
